WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.900
Good Morning Hank, It's Wednesday.

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:01.660
I'm at my in-law's house.

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:02.600
Like most of the internet,

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:04.560
I am fascinated by honey badgers,

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.420
these two to three foot long creatures that

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:07.640
weigh 30 pounds,

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.360
live here,

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:08.860
eat....

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:09.680
𝐚𝐧𝐲𝐭𝐡𝐢𝐧𝐠

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:13.800
and lead these solitary, non-monogamous lives of total badassery.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.820
But Hank, Randall's famous and crazy-ass narration

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:19.120
does nothing to capture the glory of the honey badger!

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.840
DUN DUN DUN DUN! HONEY BADGER!

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:23.300
Hank, I'm not making this up, although it is hotly debated among naturalists,

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.320
but there are lots of reports of honey badgers, which are small,

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:27.560
attacking larger prey

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.200
like wildebeest, or zebras, or water buffalo

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.080
by going straight for the nuts!

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:33.940
This is known as "emasculating your prey",

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:37.200
basically, you just bite off the balls, and then you attack....

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:37.840
the rest.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:40.640
Also, there are reports that when honey badgers attack humans,

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.720
which does happen occasionally,

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:43.440
they do go straight for the nuts.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.280
DUN DUN DUN DUN! HONEY BADGER!

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:48.140
Hank, a lot of biologists believe that honey badgers are able to attack beehives

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:52.340
because they go up to those beehives and release scent out of their anal glands,

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:55.520
which is so malodorous, that the bees run away

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:58.100
and then the honey badgers are able to take the honey.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:58.960
That's right, Hank!

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:00.260
They use a fart attack!

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.580
So not only do honey badgers have,

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:04.580
like, the most fearsome claws and teeth in the animal kingdom,

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:06.480
they also have the stinkiest farts!

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:09.280
Of course, some bees heroically stay behind and sting honey badgers,

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:10.400
but it doesn't bother them much

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.720
because they are more immune to bee venom

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.680
than almost any mammal on the planet!

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:16.600
DUN DUN DUN DUN! HONEY BADGER!

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:17.800
So Hank, do you know what cheetah cubs look like?

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:18.360
probably not,

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.820
because you probably didn't spend your entire Thanksgiving vacation

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:21.900
researching honey badgers...

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.360
they look like this.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:26.260
And many wildlife biologists speculate this is an evolutionary adaptation

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:28.540
to make baby cheetahs look like honey badgers

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:32.100
because no predator would 𝐞𝐯𝐞𝐫 want to attack a honey badger

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:33.880
unless it is absolutely desperate,

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:38.040
because honey badgers are harder to kill than 19th century Russian monks!

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:40.140
What, it's a Rasputin joke....

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:41.640
It's too obscure‽

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:42.720
C'mon!

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.200
Everybody knows Rasputin!

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:45.880
DUN DUN DUN DUN! HONEY BADGER!

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:48.160
Let's tackle the question of why honey badgers are so hard to kill,

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:50.040
so honey badgers, like an Olsen twin,

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:52.460
have more skin than seems entirely necessary

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:53.340
given their frame.

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:56.680
This loose skin-ness means that whenever you grab or bite them,

00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:58.320
there's always room for them to, like,

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.320
come around and bite you back.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:01.940
Plus their skin is incredibly thick,

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:03.480
like you can't hack through it with a machete,

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:05.160
and it's resistant to arrows!

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.740
It's like some kind of super-skin!

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:09.560
So here you are trying to bite through this super-skin creature,

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:11.360
and he's coming around and biting at your face,

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:13.800
and you're thinking, "Agh! I shoulda gotten a gazelle!"

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.720
DUN DUN DUN DUN! HONEY BADGER!

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:18.000
So all this means that the number one honey badger predator,

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:18.900
like most animals,

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:19.740
is humans!

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:22.080
Now honey badger skin is, and I'm not making this up,

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.260
can stop some bullets,

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:25.380
but you can kill them with a high-powered rifle.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:28.280
But they get us back because they often dig up human graves

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.020
and eat our ancestors!

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:31.880
DUN DUN DUN DUN! HONEY BADGER!

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:33.920
Honey badgers: Hank, they are not kidding around!

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.600
So that's what I did with my Thanksgiving vacation,

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:40.980
I also watched a lot of tape of myself playing FIFA to prepare for the FA cup final.

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:43.200
We're going back--to the FA Cup final!

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:46.540
The Swindon Town Swoodilpoopers will be facing Chelsea football club

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:49.720
and we will avenge our terrible loss in last year's FA cup final

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:50.900
and I am excited!!!

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:52.520
If you don't know what I'm talking about, link in the dooblydoo,

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.300
Hank, I hope you learned something about honey badgers,

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:55.720
I will see you on Friday.

